# Fernly Playwright page objects

## Where locators live

Locators belong in `tests/pages/*` as `readonly` fields on a page class. Specs import page objects and call actions; they do not call `page.getByRole`, `page.getByLabel`, or `page.locator` for UI.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/e2e/browse.spec.ts
const browse = new BrowsePage(page);
await browse.selectSortByLabel('Price: high to low');
await expect(browse.plantNameHeadingOnFirstCard(mostExpensive.name)).toBeVisible();
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — locator in the spec
await page.getByRole('combobox', { name: 'Sort by' }).selectOption({ label: 'Price: high to low' });
```

## Locator order (role, label, text)

Prefer `getByRole`, then `getByLabel`, then `getByText`. Do not use CSS selectors or XPath in page objects. Scope with role + name when a control has no label (promo field inside the “Have a promo code?” form).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/CartPage.ts (unnamed field — only textbox on the cart page)
this.promoCodeInput = page.getByRole('textbox');
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — tests/e2e/promo-codes.spec.ts (old pattern)
const input = page.locator('form').filter({ hasText: /Have a promo code/i }).locator('input');
```

## Actions on page classes

Expose async methods with one-line JSDoc (`@param`, `@returns`). A page object never calls `expect`. Methods return `void`, `this`, or the next page object after navigation.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/pages/CartPage.ts
async goToCheckout(): Promise<CheckoutPage> {
  await this.goToCheckoutLink.click();
  return new CheckoutPage(this.page);
}
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — assertion inside a page object
async applyPromoCode(code: string) {
  await expect(this.havePromoCodePrompt).toBeVisible();
  await this.promoCodeInput.fill(code);
}
```

## Assertions stay in the spec

Keep every `expect` in `tests/e2e` or `tests/visual`. Specs may use locators from the page object as the subject of assertions.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — tests/e2e/plant-reviews.spec.ts
await expect(plant.formAlert).toBeVisible();
await expect(plant.formAlert).toContainText(/already reviewed/i);
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — hiding an assertion in a “helper” on the page class
async expectAlreadyReviewedError() {
  await expect(this.formAlert).toContainText(/already reviewed/i);
}
```
